Every fit now carries a GOODNESS OF FIT (fix round, findings 2 and 9).  The two-template family can only produce phi shapes INSIDE the span of the cosmic and non-cosmic templates; when the data sit outside it the minimiser rails at f = 0 and the profile interval is the width of a REFUTED model, not a bound.  An interval from a fit with gof_p < 0.01 is NOT quoted and the slice is called INCONCLUSIVE.
